Can you please confirm for this MQS ID:

When was the message originally generated by MQS?
Was it successfully published to any Event Hub on the first attempt?
When was it written to Blob?
Was the record we received in BICoE on the 26th from the original publish or Blob reprocessing?
If it was reprocessed, was there also an earlier successful BICoE publish that should result in a duplicate?”

The last two questions are critical. Right now, seeing one record in BICoE on the 26th doesn't prove whether duplicate handling worked or failed—you first need to know whether two BICoE deliveries were actually expected for that MQS ID.

Ideally, for one sample ID, get them to give you this timeline:

Original generation → first publish attempt → ACK outcome → Blob write → Blob replay → BICoE delivery
